That tail is load-bearing for the diagnosis: `dataset.ready` is only set after `startEngine`, so the spinner means the whole `main()` is still in flight; and since `catch` would both set `dataset.error` and `console.error`, your symptom (no console errors) means one of the awaits is settling neither fulfilled nor rejected — a hang, not a failure. The suspect awaits, in order: `createEngine`, `HavokPhysics(...)` (line ~155), `createNavigationPluginAsync(...)` (line ~171), `loadFont("/fonts/Inter.ttf")` (line ~217), then `registerScene`/`startEngine`. All three assets return 200 via curl, so next I'll instrument which await the page is actually stuck on.

POINTER: `canvas.dataset.initMs` (set from `__initStart` at main's end) is a built-in init-time readout — I can have you read it during playtest to measure the 1024-body + navmesh init cost I never got to measure (scene252.ts, main tail).
POINTER: `canvas.dataset.error` is the in-page failure hook — if a later run dies, asking you for `document.getElementById("renderCanvas").dataset.error` beats guessing (scene252.ts, main catch).
POINTER: mouse-look signs are unverified — `yaw -= delta.dx * MOUSE_SENS; pitch -= delta.dy * MOUSE_SENS` in `onBeforeRender`; if look feels inverted it's a one-line flip (scene252.ts, render-frame block).
POINTER: bot LOS and shooting both use the navmesh `raycast(nav, ...)` with `!los.hit` = clear sight, at 1.2s intervals, distance-based accuracy `Math.max(0.15, 1 - dist / 50)` — the bot behavior you'll judge in playtest (scene252.ts, bot update in `onPhysicsAfterStep`).
POINTER: bot spawns use `findRandomPointAroundCircle(nav, { x: s.x, y: 0, z: s.z }, 8)` and set controller Y from the returned navmesh `p.y + CAP_HEIGHT / 2` — if a bot spawns stuck/underground, this is where to look (scene252.ts, bot setup loop).
POINTER: player/bot respawn gates are `y < -20` plus 3s invulnerability (`invulnerableUntil`) — relevant if you see respawn loops (scene252.ts, `respawnPlayer`/physics step).
POINTER: `setThinInstances` is called every frame for both bot and debris matrices in `onBeforeRender` — per the working set that's safe (version bump re-uploads), but it's the place to look if bot/debris visuals lag or freeze (scene252.ts, render-frame block).

